  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "The intense tension between Chef Barinov and his boss Igor Valentinovich continues to grow in the busy kitchen. The chef deliberately asks the frustrated boss to serve him another cup of tea, trying to test the man's patience and show who is really in charge.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мой чай уже закончился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, налей-ка мне чашечку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "А, он закончился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я сейчас скажу, вам принесут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, еще чаек.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Поражаюсь вам, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Как у вас все схвачено.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Стоило только подумать, вот пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ой, остыл совсем, я свежий заварю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Ничего страшного.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я не люблю горячего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как хотите, Игорь Валентинович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А я люблю горячий чай.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А, налей-ка мне чашечку.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, pour me a cup, would you?' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'pour' straight to 'small cup'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "А, он закончился.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, it is gone.' The key word here means 'he', which the speaker combines with 'ended'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я сейчас скажу, вам принесут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will ask them to bring some.' Here 'I' sets up the idea, while 'will bring' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, еще чаек.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Boss, more tea.' You'll hear 'chef' all the time in the show, here connected with 'tea'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Поражаюсь вам, Виктор Петрович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have to hand it to you, Viktor Petrovich.' Here 'be amazed' sets up the idea, while 'Petrovich' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Как у вас все схвачено.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You have got everything under control.' the speaker starts with 'how' and pairs it with 'you' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Стоило только подумать, вот пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You only had to think of it, and there it was.' Notice the word order: 'to cost' comes first, and 'to think' finishes the sentence. Chef Viktor answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ой, остыл совсем, я свежий заварю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oh, it has gone cold. I will brew a fresh pot.' In Russian, 'oh' leads into 'brew' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Ничего страшного.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That is all right.' The first content word means 'nothing', and 'terrible' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Я не люблю горячего.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not like it hot.' A compact expression built around 'I' and 'hot'. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
